<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Contract tests: they talk to a real CrowdSec LAPI over HTTP.

    This is a deliberate extension of the test strategy, not an exception
    slipped past it. The Constitution (.specify/memory/constitution.md,
    "Entwicklungsworkflow & Qualitätssicherung") says functional tests must run
    the HTTP client against static PSR-18 mocks and that no real CrowdSec
    container belongs in the pipeline. That rule stands, unedited, and the
    Functional suite still honours it — the mocks are fast, offline and
    deterministic, and nothing here replaces them.

    What the rule does not cover is the question the mocks cannot be asked. A
    hand-rolled mock answers whatever the person who wrote it believed CrowdSec
    answers. Fifty-two test files agree with that belief and would go on
    agreeing with it after CrowdSec changed its mind — the suite is green by
    construction, because both sides of the comparison come from the same
    author. The only thing that can contradict it is CrowdSec.

    Hence a separate suite, a separate configuration and a separate CI job.
    It is not called "Functional", it does not run under the Functional
    configuration, and it cannot be started by accident: without
    CROWDSEC_CONTRACT_TESTS=1 every test in it skips. Widening the
    Constitution's testing section to name this layer is the owner's call, not
    something a passing merge request should decide.
-->
<phpunit xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://schema.phpunit.de/12.0/phpunit.xsd"
         bootstrap="../vendor/autoload.php"
         cacheDirectory=".phpunit.cache"
         cacheResult="false"
         colors="true"
         failOnRisky="true"
         failOnWarning="true"
         requireCoverageMetadata="false"
>
    <testsuites>
        <testsuite name="Contract">
            <directory>Contract</directory>
        </testsuite>
    </testsuites>
    <php>
        <ini name="display_errors" value="1"/>
    </php>
</phpunit>
